SECTION 12 -- PASS 6: three cells, closed as classes.  Written BEFORE part 6 (this file's mtime
against part6/driver.log is the order witness; it is not edited after the table).
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
(1) BYTE READS REACH EVERY ARM (grok).  Odd blocks included -- a byte access skips the m88k
    alignment check -- and fall through the width guard (len == 1) to the arm's second
    predicate.  Delete it at a storing block: a byte READ stores idata == 0, while the readback
    in the same stream is served by the memcpy before the switch and prints the old value; only
    a SECOND read sees it.  "odd blocks' read side UNREACHABLE" was true of WIDE reads only (L4,
    narrowed).  Rows `brd2 *' x9 (set, read, read again -> pre), `brd pscale noig', `brd ipl
    noro'.  Outside the clause-(d) closure: L1 construction.
(2) THE LANDING CHANNEL AT LEN 4 / 8 (Opus seat, MEASURED: M1_W4FALL_ALL 118/118).  `latch all
    w'/`latch all d' count the announce; no row read a register back after a 4- or 8-byte write.
    The contract sentence "pin the REFUSAL at every block for each non-byte width" was FALSE (L4)
    and the repair was nulled at two widths (L2).  Rows `rb4 *' x9, `rb8 *' x9 (byte preset,
    put w / put d, LD_BU -> pre), `pscale noig4|8', `ipl noig4|8' (0), `latch samew|samed' (1).
    CHANNEL per row: the readback value, which differs under the fall-through mutant because
    every storing body writes a lane of idata (GENCTL/MASK/SCC*: 0xdd or 0x33; VECBASE 0xd0/0x30;
    TxCTL 0x01; TxICR 0x15).
(3) THE TIMER PENDING COUNT (Fable seat `&& !d->pending_timer2_interrupts' 118/118; Opus seat
    `&& d->pending_timer1_interrupts == 0' 118/118 -- independent measurements of one class).
    pending_timer* is a DIRECT read of the guarded TxICR body (the `> 0' tests), so clause (d)
    rule (2) puts the qualifier IN closure at that arm: L2, the pass-5 `warned' standard.  The
    field's only writer is pcc_timer_tick, a timer_add/SIGALRM callback that debugger.c stops for
    the whole of every `step' -- five passes of stepping rows could never hold it non-zero.  Rows
    `pend1 *' / `pend2 *': arm (compare 1, count 0, IEN|IL1, CEN), FREE-RUN to a breakpoint while
    the guest polls TxICR with bb0 until reassert sets INT (0x31: liveness AND device signature --
    a mis-encoded bb0 reads 0x11), then a wide write with the count non-zero.  Shape verified once
    by hand on the restored /tmp/gxopus_p6 fix binary before these rows were written: loop exit at
    CODE+0x18, r4 0x31, the st.h declined, readback 0x31.
    GUARD-FIELD / BODY-FIELD for TxICR, redone: guard reads len, writeflag; body reads
    pcctwo_reg[relative_addr] (rb*), idata (all), pending_timer1/2 (pend*), the INT bit (pend*).
    Section 1 named the field and converted only idata; that omission is what passes 5 and 6 paid
    for, and the class is now enumerated above rather than repaired one cell at a time.
